  "source_refinement": "Original predictions, bytes and failed independent1 retained under obj/parallel/nominal-unsize/refinement1. Rust no_core requires actual Index/Add roles for indexing/arithmetic and mutable DispatchFromDyn for mutable virtual methods. Refined sources use real slice-pattern reads/writes and a saturating state transition for exact single evaluation, add actual mutable DispatchFromDyn implementation, and name the outer borrow in formation-paid. Expected conversion outcomes and native observations unchanged. Independent2 slice element-binding patterns exposed missing real shared-reference Clone/Copy implementations (Rust delayed ICEs), now supplied; original no-binding controls accepted. All ICE files relocated losslessly under owning obj/independent2. Source-faithful remains byte-identical. Two predeclared explicit-goal lifetime controls distinguish equality from one-way shortening. Fixed repr(C) attachment after the inserted Dispatch impl; the failed attribute-on-impl bytes remain padded-before-refinement.rs."
